<!-- Website-only teaching for android/performance/app-size-and-r8.md; original chapter remains read-only. Sources checked 2026-10-25. -->

<!-- @opening -->

<p class="story-lead">A feature works in development and fails only in the shipped build. At the same time its SDK adds download weight. The release artifact must answer two questions: what code survived, and what did the user actually download?</p>

Track code reachability, dynamic entry points and exact-build diagnostics together.

<!-- @after Architecture :: visual -->

### The artifact is the evidence boundary

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-flow" style="--cols:3"><div class="node"><strong>Inputs</strong><small>Compiled app/library code and release configuration.</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Optimised output</strong><small>DEX, resources and native code for the delivered configuration.</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Diagnostic artifacts</strong><small>Keep the matching mapping and symbols with the release identity.</small></div></div><figcaption>Compare the same variant and device-delivery configuration. An AAB archive’s size is not the size every user downloads.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Production Example :: animation -->

### Make one release failure readable

<figure class="stepper"><span class="stepper-title">Make one release failure readable</span><div class="stage viz-grid" style="--cols:2"><div class="node" data-el="release"><strong>Release identity</strong><small>Version and exact artifact</small></div><div class="node" data-el="stack"><strong>Crash report</strong><small>Minified managed frames</small></div><div class="node" data-el="mapping"><strong>Matching mapping</strong><small>Retained by CI</small></div><div class="node" data-el="owner"><strong>Diagnosis</strong><small>Readable frame plus context</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[{"label": "Identify", "caption": "Find the precise build that produced the failure, including variant and release identity.", "state": {"release": "active"}, "add": ["release", "stack", "mapping", "owner"]}, {"label": "Match", "caption": "Locate that build’s R8 mapping. A similarly named mapping from another release is not evidence of a correct match.", "state": {"release": "done", "mapping": "active", "stack": "warn"}}, {"label": "Retrace", "caption": "Use the matching mapping to recover readable managed frames where the artifact supports it. Native frames need their own matching symbol workflow.", "state": {"mapping": "done", "stack": "active"}}, {"label": "Reproduce", "caption": "Exercise the failing journey on a release-equivalent artifact. An unminified development success cannot validate the transformed path.", "state": {"stack": "done", "owner": "active"}}]</script><figcaption>Illustrative sequence. Use Previous, Next or Play; every step is also available as text.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Staff Engineer Thinking :: staff -->

Attribute size growth to its owner and artifact bucket. Keep release diagnostics reproducible while narrowing any necessary retention rules to the actual entry points.

<!-- @before Further Reading :: check -->

### Check your diagnosis

<details><summary>Does the AAB file size equal every user’s download?</summary>

No. Delivery varies by configuration and selected modules; inspect the relevant delivered APK set.

</details>

<details><summary>Why retain mapping per build?</summary>

Retracing must match the code transformation that produced those managed frames.

</details>

<details><summary>Which test catches a release-only dynamic lookup failure?</summary>

A release-equivalent test that exercises that lookup, with the same relevant shrinking and optimisation configuration.

</details>

<!-- @before Further Reading :: deeper -->

Primary evidence for the added layer: [R8 configuration](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/enable-app-optimization), [Keep rules](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/keep-rules-overview).
